 "level_notes": {
  "0": "perl5 (github.com/Perl/perl5, branch blead) is the only complete implementation and defines the language ('only perl can parse Perl'): toke.c is a hand-written context-sensitive lexer driving the Bison grammar perly.y, op.c builds and peep.c optimizes the op tree, pp*.c hold the opcode bodies run by run.c, sv.c/av.c/hv.c/gv.c implement the value model and symbol tables, regcomp.c/regexec.c the regex engine. Perlito and cperl are partial alternatives.",
  "1": "No standard or specification: the perldoc pages shipped with perl (perlsyn, perldata, perlop, perlsub, perlre, perlobj, perlfunc, perlvar) are the official reference, and the perlNNNdelta pages are the release notes. Language changes go through PPCs (Proposed Perl Changes), introduced in 2021.",
  "2": "Programming Perl (the 'Camel book') is the classic designer-authored book but is paywalled; Modern Perl and Higher-Order Perl are free online.",
  "3": "Rosetta Code reports 'blocked' to automated checkers; metacpan.org rejects automated clients."
 },
